CORE
F12ModularTest
--function F12ModularTest.caller --modular -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
type inconsistency
--
This regression covers the DFCC-validator integration: under
--modular + --validate-goto-model + --validate-ssa-equation,
JBMC must NOT trip
  - "every function whose address is taken must be in the
     function map" (fixed by ordering remove_unused_functions
     to run after reinitialize_model in dfcc.cpp), nor
  - "<callee> type inconsistency" on JBMC's auto-injected
     <clinit_wrapper> CALL (fixed by
     dfcct::refresh_call_function_types() in dfcc.cpp).

The Java sources reuse the standard org.strata.jverify.JVerify
shape: `precondition`, `postcondition`, `assigns` are no-op
helper functions JBMC's java_bytecode_contracts pass converts
into JVerify contract clauses.
